UX Case Study: Kashmiri Essence
Project Overview

Kashmiri Essence is a conceptual digital product focused on bridging the gap between traditional Kashmiri artisans and modern consumers. 
The project explores how thoughtful UX can preserve cultural identity while solving trust, discovery, and accessibility challenges in digital commerce.

Background & Context

Kashmir has a rich legacy of handicrafts passed down through generations. Despite global demand, many artisans remain digitally invisible, 
and customers often struggle to find authentic Kashmiri products online.
Most existing platforms prioritize transactions over storytelling, 
resulting in a loss of cultural context, reduced trust, and poor user experience for both artisans and buyers.


Problem Statement

Users want to discover and purchase authentic Kashmiri handicrafts, but there is no dedicated digital platform that clearly communicates product authenticity, 
cultural significance, and artisan credibility in a simple and trustworthy way.
At the same time, artisans lack a scalable digital channel that allows them to showcase their work, share their stories, 
and reach a broader audience without relying heavily on intermediaries.

Users & Stakeholders

  Primary Users
    Customers seeking authentic Kashmiri handicrafts and lifestyle products
    Local Kashmiri artisans and small sellers
  Secondary Stakeholders
    Cultural preservation communities
    Ethical commerce and fair-trade advocates
    Platform administrators

Key User Pain Points
  
  Customer Pain Points
    Difficulty verifying product authenticity
    Limited understanding of cultural and historical context
    Low trust in generic e-commerce platforms
    Poor discovery experience

  Artisan Pain Points
    Limited digital visibility
    Dependence on intermediaries
    No platform to present product stories and craftsmanship
    Inconsistent branding and representation

UX Goals
  Build trust through transparency and clarity
  Improve discovery of authentic Kashmiri products
  Preserve and communicate cultural storytelling
  Create an intuitive, mobile-first experience
  Balance modern usability with cultural respect

Business Goals
  Enable direct visibility for artisans
  Reduce dependency on intermediaries
  Create a scalable and sustainable digital platform
  Support ethical and culture-driven commerce

Assumptions & Hypotheses
  Users value authenticity and cultural context when purchasing handicrafts
  Trust increases when artisan stories and product origins are clearly presented
  A focused, culturally aligned UX improves engagement and confidence
  Mobile-first design is critical for accessibility and reach

Scope & Constraints
  In Scope
    Product discovery and exploration  
    Artisan visibility and storytelling
    Trust and transparency mechanisms
  
  Out of Scope
    Logistics and supply-chain operations
    Payment gateway implementation
    Physical quality verification processes
  
  Success Metrics
    Increased user confidence in product authenticity 
    Improved engagement with artisan profiles
    Higher product discovery and exploration rates
    Positive qualitative feedback on trust and usability

Outcome (Design To Be Added)
  The design phase focuses on translating these insights into a culturally respectful, user-centered digital experience.
